# =====================================================================================
# BREACHPOINT - Tools/env.local.example
#
# This file is the COMMITTED, reviewable template. Copy it to Tools/env.local and edit
# that copy:
#
#     Copy-Item Tools\env.local.example Tools\env.local
#
# Tools/env.local is MACHINE-LOCAL and NEVER COMMITTED (docs/contracts/testing.md:
# "set per machine in Tools/env.local, never committed"). It is already listed in the
# repo .gitignore; verify with `git check-ignore -v Tools/env.local` before you ever
# `git add -A`. Nothing in it is secret, but it is a path on one workstation and it
# must not travel with the repo.
#
# Format: KEY=VALUE, one per line. '#' starts a comment. Values may be quoted.
# Do NOT quote-escape backslashes; write the Windows path literally.
# Read by Tools/_BRLadderCommon.ps1 on behalf of every ladder wrapper. There is no
# hardcoded engine path anywhere in Tools/ - if this file is missing, every wrapper
# reports BLOCKED with the reason rather than guessing.
# =====================================================================================

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ENGINE_ROOT - the root of a SOURCE-BUILT Unreal Engine 5.8 (the folder that directly
#               contains Engine\ and GenerateProjectFiles.bat).
#
# IT MUST BE A SOURCE BUILD. This is not a preference; it is why the whole ladder is
# shaped this way:
#
#   * A launcher/Epic Games Launcher install of UE 5.8 ships PRECOMPILED binaries for
#     the Editor and Game target types ONLY. It contains no UnrealServer binaries and
#     no engine source to build them from, so the BreachpointServer target CANNOT be
#     compiled against it - UBT fails looking for server-configuration engine libs.
#   * testing.md requires all three targets (BreachpointEditor, Breachpoint,
#     BreachpointServer) to compile on EVERY rung-1 run, and rung 4 (Gauntlet) launches
#     a real dedicated server. Both die without a source build.
#   * See docs/BREACHPOINT-GAMELIFT-PLAN.md section 1 and TICKET_BP00's Log - this was verified
#     on this machine, not assumed: the launcher 5.8.1 install had no UnrealServer
#     target under Engine/Intermediate/Build/Win64/x64/ at all.
#
# How to tell whether a candidate path is a source build (do this, don't guess):
#   1. <ENGINE_ROOT>\Engine\Build\SourceDistribution.txt   EXISTS  -> source build
#      (a launcher install has Engine\Build\InstalledBuild.txt instead)
#   2. <ENGINE_ROOT>\Engine\Source\Runtime\Engine\Private\  is populated -> source present
#   3. <ENGINE_ROOT>\Engine\Binaries\Win64\UnrealEditor.exe exists -> the engine has
#      actually been built at least once (cloning the source is not enough)
# Tools\run-ubt.ps1 checks (1) and warns if the marker is missing, because a launcher
# install produces a confusing UBT error hours into a run rather than a clear one now.
#
# How to find it:
#   * You built it yourself: it is wherever you cloned UnrealEngine and ran
#     Setup.bat -> GenerateProjectFiles.bat -> built UE5 in Visual Studio.
#   * Registry of registered engine installations (source builds register a GUID that
#     matches the "EngineAssociation" GUID in Breachpoint.uproject):
#       Get-ItemProperty 'HKCU:\Software\Epic Games\Unreal Engine\Builds'
#     The value whose NAME equals the uproject's EngineAssociation GUID is this project's
#     engine; its DATA is the path to put below.
#   * Sanity check the version:  <ENGINE_ROOT>\Engine\Build\Build.version  ->  "MajorVersion": 5,
#     "MinorVersion": 8. A 5.5 or 5.6 source build will not do; the project targets 5.8.
#
# No trailing backslash. Spaces in the path are fine and must NOT be quoted-escaped.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ENGINE_ROOT=D:\Path\To\Your\UnrealEngine_5.8_Source

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional overrides. Every one of these has a working default; set them only if this
# machine differs. Unknown keys are ignored, so leaving them commented costs nothing.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where rung logs are written. Default: Tools\Logs (self-gitignored).
# LOG_DIR=D:\Path\To\BreachpointLadderLogs

# Minutes before a rung-2 spec run is killed and reported FAIL(timeout).
# Default 20. Raise on a cold DDC - the first -nullrhi editor launch can take a while.
# SPEC_TIMEOUT_MINUTES=20

# Minutes before a rung-4 Gauntlet run is killed. Default 30.
# GAUNTLET_TIMEOUT_MINUTES=30
